  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Dribble and pass in three lines",
  "description": "Three rows with a cone at each end and one in the middle, about 15 metres between the ends. The players line up at the end cones, one ball per row. The first player dribbles to the middle cone, passes to the team-mate at the other end, then runs after the ball and joins the back of that line. The receiver does the same back.\n\nMake it harder with the weaker foot, or by passing straight from the first cone. Works well for young children, from about 7 years old. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Dribble with small touches and look up now and then."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stop the ball at the middle cone before you pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Receiver: move towards the ball and receive with the inside of your foot."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
